     "D-Day"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "World War II (1939-1945) began when Germany invaded Poland. It was fought between the Allies (Britain, France, the USSR, the USA) and the Axis (Germany, Italy, Japan). Germany swept through Europe with a fast attack called blitzkrieg.\nThe war spread when Germany attacked the USSR in 1941 and Japan attacked Pearl Harbor, bringing in the USA. The tide turned at Stalingrad and in the D-Day landings of 1944. Germany surrendered in May 1945.\nThe USA dropped atomic bombs on Hiroshima and Nagasaki in August 1945, and Japan surrendered. Millions were killed, including the Jews in the Holocaust. The cost made the world seek lasting peace."
    }
